    "answer": {
      "short": "a and f; b and g; c and e; d and h.",
      "worked": "Reading the coefficient of $x$ after making $y$ the subject gives:\n$$\\begin{aligned}y&=-\\frac34x+\\frac74 &&\\text{(b)}\\\\y&=\\frac13x+\\frac53 &&\\text{(d)}\\\\y&=-\\frac12x+\\frac72 &&\\text{(f)}\\\\y&=\\frac43x+\\frac83 &&\\text{(g)}\\end{aligned}$$\nThe gradients of a–h are respectively $2,-\\frac34,1,\\frac13,-1,-\\frac12,\\frac43,-3$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}m_am_f&=2\\left(-\\frac12\\right)=-1\\\\m_bm_g&=-\\frac34\\times\\frac43=-1\\\\m_cm_e&=1(-1)=-1\\\\m_dm_h&=\\frac13(-3)=-1\\end{aligned}$$\nTherefore the perpendicular pairs are a and f, b and g, c and e, and d and h.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
